{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "02772",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 1.38,
      "end_seconds": 4.47,
      "duration_seconds": 3.09,
      "text": "sorry, doctor, shall I sit here?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 5.67,
      "end_seconds": 10.35,
      "duration_seconds": 4.68,
      "text": "so, yes, have a seat. Tell me what's going on"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 11.07,
      "end_seconds": 15.76,
      "duration_seconds": 4.69,
      "text": "Good morning, doctor. I came along to help out."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 16.26,
      "end_seconds": 19.07,
      "duration_seconds": 2.81,
      "text": "please do extra information is always welcome"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 19.59,
      "end_seconds": 26.31,
      "duration_seconds": 6.72,
      "text": "It's, It's fainting on exertion, doctor. She didn't want to come, but I insisted."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 28.19,
      "end_seconds": 29.47,
      "duration_seconds": 1.28,
      "text": "since when exactly?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 30.5,
      "end_seconds": 35.08,
      "duration_seconds": 4.58,
      "text": "well, it's been going on for ten days"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 36.06,
      "end_seconds": 44.83,
      "duration_seconds": 8.77,
      "text": "Can you describe it a bit more for me? How strong it is, what the pattern is, what helps."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 46.03,
      "end_seconds": 70.11,
      "duration_seconds": 24.08,
      "text": "I'd say every other day. About a eight out of ten. It's worse with exertion. I kept putting it it off, which I know isn't sensible. Oh, as for swollen ankles, I honestly can't say when that began. It might have been last month or the month before."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 71.1,
      "end_seconds": 74.32,
      "duration_seconds": 3.22,
      "text": "would you say mild moderate or severe?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 75.28,
      "end_seconds": 81.56,
      "duration_seconds": 6.28,
      "text": "A three out of ten, I suppose. There's being very breathless as well."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 83.44,
      "end_seconds": 86.74,
      "duration_seconds": 3.3,
      "text": "would you say mild, moderate or severe?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 87.53,
      "end_seconds": 89.01,
      "duration_seconds": 1.48,
      "text": "it's severe, honestly"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 91.09,
      "end_seconds": 94.08,
      "duration_seconds": 2.99,
      "text": "Have you had fever, by any chance?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 95.02,
      "end_seconds": 96.73,
      "duration_seconds": 1.71,
      "text": "nope, no fever"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 97.86,
      "end_seconds": 102.27,
      "duration_seconds": 4.41,
      "text": "actually doctor I did notice fever. She doesn't always say"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 102.97,
      "end_seconds": 109.77,
      "duration_seconds": 6.8,
      "text": "No um I don't think I did. Maybe a little I'm not sure."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 111.81,
      "end_seconds": 119.76,
      "duration_seconds": 7.95,
      "text": "Alright, I'll note both what you've said and what you've noticed. Any cough or leg pain at all?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 121.22,
      "end_seconds": 125.14,
      "duration_seconds": 3.92,
      "text": "I haven't had cough or leg pain, no"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 128.11,
      "end_seconds": 130.28,
      "duration_seconds": 2.17,
      "text": "Is your mobility otherwise okay?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 131.43,
      "end_seconds": 133.12,
      "duration_seconds": 1.69,
      "text": "no, nothing there"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 134.37,
      "end_seconds": 137.88,
      "duration_seconds": 3.51,
      "text": "Right, anything different when you pass water?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 139.87,
      "end_seconds": 141.46,
      "duration_seconds": 1.59,
      "text": "nothing there, no"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 143.04,
      "end_seconds": 145.81,
      "duration_seconds": 2.77,
      "text": "so, anything surgical in your history?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 147.51,
      "end_seconds": 152.61,
      "duration_seconds": 5.1,
      "text": "yes, I had part of my thyroid removed, years back"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 166.29,
      "end_seconds": 168.74,
      "duration_seconds": 2.45,
      "text": "tell me your medicines, please"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 169.86,
      "end_seconds": 177.61,
      "duration_seconds": 7.75,
      "text": "I'm on hydrocortisone cream, when needed for the eczema. Amlodipine, 5 milligrams, once a day"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 178.26,
      "end_seconds": 181.84,
      "duration_seconds": 3.58,
      "text": "Okay, how long has that been going on?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 183.42,
      "end_seconds": 194.21,
      "duration_seconds": 10.79,
      "text": "For about three months. Simvastatin. I take it 20 milligrams, at night. A neighbour of mine said I should see someone about it."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 195.03,
      "end_seconds": 196.97,
      "duration_seconds": 1.94,
      "text": "and for how long?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 198.43,
      "end_seconds": 202.57,
      "duration_seconds": 4.14,
      "text": "Two years now. I take furosemide, every morning"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 204.17,
      "end_seconds": 206.64,
      "duration_seconds": 2.47,
      "text": "How much do you take?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 207.83,
      "end_seconds": 209.2,
      "duration_seconds": 1.37,
      "text": "it's 40 milligrams"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 217.97,
      "end_seconds": 221.3,
      "duration_seconds": 3.33,
      "text": "Has anyone ever diagnosed you with something?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 222.76,
      "end_seconds": 243.78,
      "duration_seconds": 21.02,
      "text": "yes eczema sorry I know I'm rambling a bit my family kept telling me to get it checked i've had high blood pressure for about ten years now i'd rather not end up on lots of tablets if I can avoid it"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 244.37,
      "end_seconds": 245.8,
      "duration_seconds": 1.43,
      "text": "is that everything?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 246.64,
      "end_seconds": 253.65,
      "duration_seconds": 7.01,
      "text": "I've had high cholesterol yes. Uh I have heart failure for two years"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 254.4,
      "end_seconds": 268.03,
      "duration_seconds": 13.63,
      "text": "right so eczema and high blood pressure are already on your record we'll keep that in mind today has anything ever caused you a reaction? I mean any allergies take your time there's no rush"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 269.14,
      "end_seconds": 270.93,
      "duration_seconds": 1.79,
      "text": "no allergies at all"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 272.07,
      "end_seconds": 274.99,
      "duration_seconds": 2.92,
      "text": "a few questions about your lifestyle now"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 275.53,
      "end_seconds": 288.4,
      "duration_seconds": 12.87,
      "text": "My husband and I live above the shop. I walk the dog every morning. I retired from the post office two years ago."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0042",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 302.84,
      "end_seconds": 305.89,
      "duration_seconds": 3.05,
      "text": "Are there any illnesses in your family?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0043",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 306.92,
      "end_seconds": 309.64,
      "duration_seconds": 2.72,
      "text": "my mother has an underactive thyroid"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0044",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 313.48,
      "end_seconds": 316.61,
      "duration_seconds": 3.13,
      "text": "I'll just record a few vital signs."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0045",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 323.38,
      "end_seconds": 325.58,
      "duration_seconds": 2.2,
      "text": "sit still for a moment.."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0046",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 338.63,
      "end_seconds": 347.14,
      "duration_seconds": 8.51,
      "text": "Okay: SpO2 93 percent on room air, heart rate 87. And BP is 130 over 90, temperature 37.4."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0047",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 351.11,
      "end_seconds": 353.11,
      "duration_seconds": 2.0,
      "text": "is that alright, doctor?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0048",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 354.31,
      "end_seconds": 356.77,
      "duration_seconds": 2.46,
      "text": "I'll come back to the numbers"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0049",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 359.52,
      "end_seconds": 362.09,
      "duration_seconds": 2.57,
      "text": "Let's move on to the examination."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0050",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 363.97,
      "end_seconds": 366.11,
      "duration_seconds": 2.14,
      "text": "hold that for a second"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0051",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 375.9,
      "end_seconds": 381.57,
      "duration_seconds": 5.67,
      "text": "there is a loud second heart sound and a raised jugular pulse"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0052",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 383.98,
      "end_seconds": 405.89,
      "duration_seconds": 21.91,
      "text": "please sit back down so, based on the history and the examination, it points towards possible pulmonary hypertension i'd also keep chronic clots in the lungs in mind stop me if I've got anything wrong you've had fainting on exertion for ten days, and no leg pain"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0053",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 406.48,
      "end_seconds": 407.88,
      "duration_seconds": 1.4,
      "text": "Yes that's right."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0054",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 408.94,
      "end_seconds": 422.46,
      "duration_seconds": 13.52,
      "text": "I'm going to order blood tests for breathlessness. The result will help us decide whether anything more is needed. I'm going to to order an echocardiogram for exertional syncope."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0055",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 423.55,
      "end_seconds": 425.01,
      "duration_seconds": 1.46,
      "text": "that makes sense"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0056",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 425.94,
      "end_seconds": 440.95,
      "duration_seconds": 15.01,
      "text": "no exertion for now I am arranging urgent specialist tests one warning sign to remember: the symptoms get worse in that that case don't wait anything else on your mind before you go?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0057",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 446.17,
      "end_seconds": 449.12,
      "duration_seconds": 2.95,
      "text": "uh, alright, thanks, take care"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0058",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 450.01,
      "end_seconds": 451.62,
      "duration_seconds": 1.61,
      "text": "Have a good day."
    }
  ]
}